%T A400884 146,146,169,172,202,202,229,229,236,266,306,309,309,320,389,392,397,
%U A400884 397,434,483,483,483,542,542,592,603,663,666,666,714,764,764,771,771,906,909,909,919,974,1056
%N A400884 a(n) is the number of distinct placements of two nonoverlapping similar Pythagorean triangles whose acute angles meet to form a right angle at a corner of an n X n square.
%C A400884 The objective is to form a complete right angle at a single corner of an n X n square using two non-overlapping, similar Pythagorean triangles, possibly of different sizes. Their complementary acute angles must meet at that corner and together form 90 degrees; merely touching the corner is insufficient. Both triangles must lie entirely within the square, with one side of each triangle along a different adjacent side of the square. Placing triangles at separate corners or using a triangle's right angle at the chosen corner is not permitted. Empty space elsewhere is allowed. Distinct configurations are counted up to reflections, according to the side lengths and orientations of the triangles forming the corner.
%H A400884 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A400884/b400884.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A400884 Benoit Cloitre, <a href="/A400884/a400884_2.pdf">Asymptptoic behavior of A400884</a>
%H A400884 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A400884/a400884_1.pdf">pdf for illustration n = 8</a>
%H A400884 Janaka Rodrigo, <a href="/A400884/a400884_6.txt">Python code for A400884</a>
%F A400884 a(n) = K*n^2 + O(n*log(n)), where K = Sum_{(x,y,z)} (1/y + 1/z)^2 = 0.27803462637..., the sum being over the primitive Pythagorean triples (x,y,z) with x^2 + y^2 = z^2 and x < y. More precisely, |a(n) - K*n^2| <= (16/3)*n*log(n) + (32/3)*n for n >= 1. Conjecture: a(n) = K*n^2 - ((4*log(1+sqrt(2)) + Pi)/Pi^2)*n*log(n) + O(n). - _Benoit Cloitre_, Nov 08 2026
%e A400884 For n = 8, there are two Pythagorean triples (3,4,5) and (6,8,10) involved in filling a corner of a square of side length 8; M = 2 + 2*C(2,2) = 2 + 2 = 4, N = 3*(1 + 2*C(1,2)) = 3*(1 + 0) = 3, R = 2*1*1 = 2. Therefore a(8) = M + N + R = 9.
%o A400884 (PARI) a(n)=sum(x=1, n-1, sum(y=x+1, n, if(issquare(x^2+y^2) && gcd(x,y)==1, my(z=sqrtint(x^2+y^2)); (n\y + n\z)^2))) \\ _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 29 2026
